      "problem": "If $f(x)=A\\cdot {2}^{x}$ and $f(6)=192,$ then $A=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "We substitute $x=6$ and $f(x)=192$ into the expression for $f(x)$ and then solve for $A,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}192 & =A\\cdot {2}^{6} \\\\ \\frac{192}{{2}^{6}} & =A \\\\ \\frac{192}{64} & =A \\\\ 3 & =A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A=3.$",
